Chapter: UsbKbdHub2
  cites Works chapter GopUsb
  cites Works chapter GopUsbKbd
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 A keyboard two hubs down, which is where the translator arithmetic
 stops being obvious.

 `usb-kbd-hub` puts a full-speed keyboard directly below a high-speed
 hub, and there the answer is easy: the hub it is plugged into owns the
 transaction translator, so reading the immediate parent is right. This
 test puts a FULL-SPEED hub in between. A full-speed hub has no
 translator of its own -- there is nothing to translate at full speed --
 so the keyboard below it is still served by the high-speed hub two
 tiers up, and the slot context must name THAT hub.

 A walk that reads the translator off the immediate parent finds a
 full-speed hub, concludes there is no translator, and writes zero. The
 device then enumerates perfectly, answers every control transfer, and
 never delivers an interrupt transfer, because the controller declines
 to schedule a periodic endpoint on a full-speed slot that names no
 translator. That is the same silent-keyboard shape as the one-tier
 case, reached by a different mistake, and it is ordinary hardware: a
 monitor hub in front of a keyboard hub is exactly this topology.

 The root keyboard is unplugged (`-xhci-no-root-kbd`) because the walk
 takes the first keyboard it finds and the root ports come first.

 What each line proves. `route=17` is 0x11: port 1 of tier 0, then port
 1 of tier 1, one nibble per tier -- it says the keyboard was reached
 through TWO hubs and not one, without which this test is `usb-kbd-hub`
 wearing a different name. `speed=1` says full speed, so a translator is
 genuinely required. `ttslot-set=1` says the walk named one. `phase=2`
 is the completion actually arriving, and it is the whole question:
 the model refuses to service the endpoint otherwise, exactly as
 silicon does.

Section: Test

  found-line : UsbKbd -> Text
  found-line (k) =
    "kbd: ok=" & (if k.uk-ok then "1" else "0")
      & " dci=" & show (k.uk-dci)
      & " speed=" & show ((k.uk-dev).ud-speed)
      & " route=" & show ((k.uk-dev).ud-route)
      & " ttslot-set=" & (if (k.uk-dev).ud-tt-slot /= 0 then "1" else "0")
      & " ttport=" & show ((k.uk-dev).ud-tt-port)

  phase-of : UsbKbd -> Integer
  phase-of (k) = peek-32 (k.uk-state) 0

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    att <- usb-attach
    print-line-uni (found-line (att.ua-kbd))
    if (att.ua-kbd).uk-ok then act
      let p0 = kbd-pump (att.ua-kbd)
      in print-line-uni ("after-arm: phase=" & show (phase-of (att.ua-kbd)))
      let p1 = kbd-pump (att.ua-kbd)
      in print-line-uni ("after-check: phase=" & show (phase-of (att.ua-kbd)))
    end
    else print-line-uni "after-arm: SKIPPED (no keyboard)"
  end
